-**Image C-deletion evidence, two scenes only.** We separately compare 20 minus_C models with 20 existing Full checkpoints for IID Benign and IID F Flip, ten matched seeds per scene. The C mask removes the scoring contribution while leaving geometric hard filtering enabled; it does not delete prediction calibration. Each model supplies all metrics and raw/native/shared views from the same round-70 checkpoint. Paired native/shared ACC/AEOD/ASPD differences (minus_C−Full) are -0.083±1.378 / +0.00292±0.01315 / -0.00142±0.01953 for IID Benign and +0.518±0.814 / +0.00139±0.01487 / +0.01098±0.02176 for IID F Flip, with ACC in percentage points. For F Flip, raw differences are +0.530±0.875 / +0.00465±0.01053 / +0.00703±0.01157. Thus the F Flip ten-seed deletion improves accuracy but raises both measured disparities; these are paired means ± sample SD, not significance or necessity claims. The native/shared F Flip AEOD difference changes from the ten-seed positive mean to +0.00025±0.01530 for nine seeds and -0.00291±0.01773 for six seeds. [The accepted two-scene table](E:/OneDrive/文档/GuardFed/docs/server_deployment_20260923/training_20260923/celeba_mechanism_v1/three_view_C_two_scenes_20261009/snapshot/TABLES.md) retains every Full/C mean, paired difference and the fixed 10/9/6-seed raw/native/shared panels. Native/shared metrics and group counts coincide for all 40 records; they are not independent calibration replications. The other eight C scenes and six other image controls remain incomplete, leaving seven image-control variants incomplete. These two scenes do not support a claim that every term is necessary or a causal explanation of dataset-dependent behavior.
